Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?[es]=20AGREEMENT=5FPRONOUNSUBJECT=5FVERB:=20fla?=
 =?UTF-8?q?g=20=C2=ABt=C3=BA=C2=BB=20with=20a=20voseo=20verb=20form?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rule for «tú» matches verb forms tagged V.[^M].[13].. or V.[^M].2P., so
person-2 voseo forms (number V, e.g. tenés = VMIP2V0) fall through the
alternation and «Tú tenés que venir.» gets no match, while the mirror case
(«Vos tienes razón.») is already flagged by the rules for «vos» in the same
group.

Mixing «tú» with a voseo verb form is an error in every variant, so this only
adds 2[PV] to the existing alternation. Ambiguous forms that are identical in
tuteo (estás, vas) are already tagged V...2S. and stay excluded by the
existing exception, and imperatives keep being excluded by the existing
antipattern («Tú marchá.»).

SpanishPatternRuleTest passes (1670 rules). Checked against a local server:
Tú tenés → tienes, Tú sos → eres, Tú querés → quieres, Tú sabés → sabes; no
match for Tú tienes / Tú estás / Tú vas / Tú marchá / Tú siéntate / Vos tenés.
No new matches over a 783k-word es-AR fiction corpus (no false positives).
---
 .../src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml  | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml b/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
index 72dba10..15f7796 100644
--- a/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
+++ b/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
@@ -24942,12 +24942,14 @@ Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
                     <token>tú<exception postag="SP.*|CC|LOC_PREP" postag_regexp="yes" scope="previous"/></token>
                     <token postag="RG|LOC_ADV" postag_regexp="yes" min="0" max="3"><exception postag="C.*" postag_regexp="yes"/></token>
                     <marker>
-                        <token postag="V.[^M].[13]..|V.[^M].2P." postag_regexp="yes"><exception postag="V...2S.|AQ.*|RG|LOC_ADV" postag_regexp="yes"/></token>
+                        <token postag="V.[^M].[13]..|V.[^M].2[PV]." postag_regexp="yes"><exception postag="V...2S.|AQ.*|RG|LOC_ADV" postag_regexp="yes"/></token>
                     </marker>
                 </pattern>
                 <message>Posible falta de concordancia entre «\1» y «\3».</message>
                 <suggestion><match no="3" postag="(V.[^M].).*" postag_regexp="yes" postag_replace="$12S."/></suggestion>
                 <example correction="vengas|vienes">Tú <marker>vengo</marker></example>
+                <example correction="tienes">Tú <marker>tenés</marker> que venir.</example>
+                <example correction="eres">Tú <marker>sos</marker> el que se queja.</example>
                 <!-- TODO: it should suggest: estéis 
                 <example correction="estés">Que tu familia y tú <marker>estén</marker>.</example>-->
                 <example>Tú vienes</example>
